{
  "name": "Pipe Otter",
  "description": "Original gacha-style figure: a sleek chocolate otter popping out of a weathered copper-and-brass standpipe with verdigris patina, bolted flanges and a red valve wheel; its tail pokes out of the side branch. Rigged with popup, idle and wave clips.",
  "notes": "Rig: riser (root, pipe frame: +X = side branch) > body_0..2 (otter chain; body_0 position.y drops the whole otter into the pipe, -15.6 = fully hidden) > head > eyes/muzzle/nose/ears/whiskers; arm_0..1 + paw (mirrored chains); tail_0..4 (chain out of the branch). The riser is 13 wide so the ducked otter (head squeezed, whiskers folded, hands up) stays inside it. On the near-vertical body loft `around` 0 is the back, so the shoulders attach at 0.33.",
